<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kiel mutiny</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as naval mutiny at Kiel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> mutiny was a revolt by sailors of the German High Seas Fleet in 1918, sparked by orders for a final naval sortie against the British at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. The unrest spread rapidly to other cities, giving rise to workers' and soldiers' councils. It triggered the German Revolution that led to the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a> and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kiel-mutiny.jpg" alt="Kiel mutiny" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-J0908-0600-002,_Novemberrevolution,_Matrosenaufstand.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
